==English==
{{wp|<dab>}}
{{number box|en|2}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sekʷ-|id=follow}}
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:secunde<id:in array>|id=order|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|secunde}}, {{m|enm|second}}, {{m|enm|secound}}, {{m|enm|secund}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|second}}, {{m|fro|seond}}, from {{der|en|la|secundus||following, next in order}}, from root of {{m|la|sequor||to follow}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*sekʷ-||to follow}}. {{doublet|en|secund|secundo}}. Displaced native {{m|en|twoth}} and partially displaced native {{m|en|other}} (from {{noncog|ang|ōþer|t=other; next; second}}).

====Alternative forms====
* {{sense|number-two}} {{alter|en|2nd|2ⁿᵈ|2d|2ᵈ|IInd}}
* {{sense|number-two}} {{alter|en|II|II.||in the names of monarchs and popes}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛk.ənd/|a=GA}}, {{enPR|sĕʹkənd}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-2nd.ogg|a=US}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-second.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛk.ənt/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛk.ən/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛk.ənd/|a=RP}}
** {{audio|en|en-uk-a second.ogg|a=UK|text=a second}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛk.ɪnd/|a=Canada}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛkənd|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|sec|ond}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# Number-[[two]]; following after the [[first]] one with nothing between them. {{non-gloss|The ordinal number corresponding to the cardinal number [[two]].}}
#: {{ux|en|He lives on '''Second''' Street.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''second''' volume in "The Lord of the Rings" series is called "The Two Towers".}}
#: {{ux|en| He became the '''second''' player to hit 50000 runs for his county.}}
#: {{ux|en|You take the first one, and I'll have the '''second'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|Eye Witness|249|The story struck the depressingly familiar note with which true stories ring in the tried ears of experienced policemen.{{...}}The '''second''' note, the high alarum, not so familiar and always important since it indicates the paramount sin in Man's private calendar, took most of them by surprise although they had been well prepared.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=John Malathronas|title=Which languages are easiest – and most difficult – for native English speakers to learn?|url=https://www.cnn.com/travel/article/learn-a-foreign-language-wellness|date=2021-04-25|passage=Malay is the lingua franca of several Southeast Asia countries and has been simplified by its use as a '''second''' language by non-native speakers.<br>For example, the Malay plural is formed by repeating a word twice – buku means book and buku-buku means books.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220322023413/https://www.cnn.com/travel/article/learn-a-foreign-language-wellness}}
#* {{quote-web|en|title=2023 Laws of Chess|url=https://rcc.fide.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/20230101Laws-of-Chess.pdf|year=2022|page=21|work=w:FIDE|passage=Consequently, in the initial position the white pieces and pawns are placed on the first and '''second''' ranks; the black pieces and pawns on the eighth and seventh ranks.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250316122506/https://rcc.fide.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/20230101Laws-of-Chess.pdf}}
# Next to the first in value, power, excellence, dignity, or rank; [[secondary]]; [[subordinate]]; [[inferior]].
#: {{ux|en|His job is '''second''' priority, because his family is the most important thing in his life.}}
#* {{RQ:Landor Imaginary Conversations|I|conv=I|Richard I and the Abbot of Boxley|6|May the day when we become the '''second''' people upon earth {{...}} be the day of our utter extirpation!}}
# Being of the same kind as one that has [[precede]]d; [[another]].
#: {{ux|en|Residents of Texas prepared for Hurricane Harvey, which would in some ways turn out to become the '''second''' Hurricane Katrina.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|IV|i|180|2|passage=A ''Daniel'' ſtill ſay I, a '''ſecond''' ''Daniel'',{{...}}}}

